<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-melanogaster-turing-wavelength-s0-morphometric-validation> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Drosophila melanogaster Schnakenberg Turing wavelength at 2.736 µm (Holocene, 0 Ma) — Morphometric validation: 88/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Dispersion r = 0.9999999989, RMSE = 4.62e-5, FFT wavelength 2.799 µm versus 2.736 µm. Pass 2 sweeps the specimen luminance quantile from 0.55 to 0.85: foreground fraction spans 0.154 (0.443 to 0.598) while circularity stays between 0.032 and 0.087, so the not-a-circle reading is stable and the area fraction is threshold-sensitive. Mode-seeded nonlinear gaps keep the chronospecies order. The KS residual statistic remains 0.726 against an independent normal. Both Pass 1 measurement gaps (single mask threshold; no saturated chronospecies run) are closed." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
