<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-melanogaster-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Drosophila melanogaster Schnakenberg Turing wavelength at 2.736 µm (Holocene, 0 Ma) — MorphoEval overall 86.7/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 2 keeps the Pass 1 Schnakenberg system (gamma solved for lambda = 2.736 µm at 0 Ma; miranda 2.242 µm; mauritiana 3.243 µm). Dispersion Pearson r = 0.9999999989, RMSE = 4.62e-5, nonlinear 2D FFT wavelength 2.799 µm, CV similarity 96.0 on a 16-frame 768x576 GIF. The mask quantile sweep (0.55 to 0.85) moves foreground fraction by 0.154 while contour circularity stays between 0.032 and 0.087. Mode-seeded 1D saturation preserves miranda 2.182 < melanogaster 2.667 < mauritiana 3.429 µm. Broadband-noise saturation does not preserve that order. Overall 86.7/100 (faithfulness 86.7, reproducibility 86.8); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 0c76d15d14afcec6c366e1b9274a6586a0de48fc; environment: . Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 90, Morphological realism / specimen match 82, Parameter expressivity 90, Morphometric validation 88, Source and data traceability 90, Code-to-model traceability 84, Reproducibility package 86. Output judged: docs/media/drosophila_melanogaster_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-melanogaster-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 0c76d15d14afcec6c366e1b9274a6586a0de48fc, image/png, 422992 B, 1488×1104 px, artifact_sha256 a5198e44d82533312ce2e385854f8ba7c3d9601826b8b99d7df8ea883615039b (sha256 a5198e44d82533312ce2e385854f8ba7c3d9601826b8b99d7df8ea883615039b), spec_fingerprint 995c7441a1e86dd55fbe8e523c9fea39052280d57b46ba75e4b98b1e0c116683. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 995c7441a1e86dd55fbe8e523c9fea39052280d57b46ba75e4b98b1e0c116683; artifact_sha256: a5198e44d82533312ce2e385854f8ba7c3d9601826b8b99d7df8ea883615039b; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/drosophila_melanogaster_turing_wavelength_s0/Drosophila_melanogaster_specimen.jpg=2a66a100d8405cc9..., datasets/drosophila_melanogaster_turing_wavelength_s0/drosophila_melanogaster_turing_wavelength_s0_reference.json=553df65dcc62824e...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-27-drosophila-melanogaster-turing-wavelength-s0-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing (1952) selects a finite wavelength by diffusion-driven instability. | Schnakenberg (1979) kinetics are f = a - u + u^2 v and g = b - u^2 v. | Wittkopp, True and Carroll (2002) place Drosophila melanin via Yellow and Ebony. | True et al. (1997) quantify morphological divergence of D. mauritiana from the simulans complex. | Richards et al. (2005) compare the D. pseudoobscura genome with D. melanogaster. | The Karwath photograph is an adult male D. melanogaster under CC BY-SA 2.5.; reconstructed_in_script: Gamma = 1.032078 is solved so argmax sigma(k) = 2 pi / 2.736 per micrometre. | Mauritiana and miranda wavelengths at that shared gamma, linear and mode-seeded. | Mask quantile sweep and the noise-seeded negative control. | Registration amplitude 0.16 on the Karwath photograph.; transfer_boundary: 2.736 µm is the assigned detail scale, not a published granule spacing. | Chronospecies wavelengths are reconstructions, not measurements from True 1997 or Richards 2005. | Richards 2005 is the pseudoobscura genome, used only as obscura-clade context for miranda.; does_not_claim: That adult abdominal stripes or ommatidia have wavelength 2.736 µm. | That broadband noise selects the linear critical wavelength. It does not, in the 1D control. | That the spot lattice is a photograph of an ocellus. | A second independent assessor, or a signed nanopub (no ~/.nanopub/profile.yml).." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: Residual, not a Pass 1 gap: broadband-noise 1D saturation does not preserve miranda < melanogaster < mauritiana. The mode-seeded saturation does.",
        "remediation needed: Residual: no second assessor, and no electron micrograph at 2.7 µm. The 2.736 µm target remains an assigned detail scale." ;
    pk:hasScore 8.67e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-melanogaster-turing-wavelength-s0-parameter-expressivity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Drosophila melanogaster Schnakenberg Turing wavelength at 2.736 µm (Holocene, 0 Ma) — Parameter expressivity: 90/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Gamma scales 0.65 to 2.05 still move analytic lambda strictly from 3.394 µm to 1.911 µm. Pass 2 adds saturated 1D runs on a shared 24 µm domain. With a cos(k_c x) seed the wavelengths are miranda 2.182, melanogaster 2.667, mauritiana 3.429 µm, so the linear order survives saturation. With broadband noise the order does not survive (noise_order_holds = 0). That negative control is why this score is 90 rather than the mid-90s. The Pass 1 gap (linear k_c only) is closed." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-parameter-expressivity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/parameter-expressivity" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-melanogaster-turing-wavelength-s0-parameter-expressivity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-melanogaster-turing-wavelength-s0-parameter-expressivity-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-melanogaster-turing-wavelength-s0-parameter-expressivity-3> ;
    pk:hasScore 9e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

