<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-melanogaster-turing-wavelength-s0> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Drosophila melanogaster Schnakenberg Turing wavelength at 2.736 µm (Holocene, 0 Ma) (Drosophila melanogaster)",
        "Drosophila melanogaster Schnakenberg Turing wavelength at 2.736 µm (Holocene, 0 Ma) faithfully reproduces Drosophila melanogaster morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-drosophila-melanogaster-turing-wavelength-s0-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-drosophila-melanogaster-turing-wavelength-s0-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-drosophila-melanogaster-turing-wavelength-s0-3> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-melanogaster-turing-wavelength-s0.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Drosophila melanogaster specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-melanogaster-turing-wavelength-s0.py> ;
    schema:about "Drosophila melanogaster" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: A second independent assessor, or a signed nanopub (no ~/.nanopub/profile.yml).",
        "does_not_claim: That adult abdominal stripes or ommatidia have wavelength 2.736 µm.",
        "does_not_claim: That broadband noise selects the linear critical wavelength. It does not, in the 1D control.",
        "does_not_claim: That the spot lattice is a photograph of an ocellus.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Gamma = 1.032078 is solved so argmax sigma(k) = 2 pi / 2.736 per micrometre.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Mask quantile sweep and the noise-seeded negative control.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Mauritiana and miranda wavelengths at that shared gamma, linear and mode-seeded.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Registration amplitude 0.16 on the Karwath photograph.",
        "reported_in_source: Richards et al. (2005) compare the D. pseudoobscura genome with D. melanogaster.",
        "reported_in_source: Schnakenberg (1979) kinetics are f = a - u + u^2 v and g = b - u^2 v.",
        "reported_in_source: The Karwath photograph is an adult male D. melanogaster under CC BY-SA 2.5.",
        "reported_in_source: True et al. (1997) quantify morphological divergence of D. mauritiana from the simulans complex.",
        "reported_in_source: Turing (1952) selects a finite wavelength by diffusion-driven instability.",
        "reported_in_source: Wittkopp, True and Carroll (2002) place Drosophila melanin via Yellow and Ebony.",
        "transfer_boundary: 2.736 µm is the assigned detail scale, not a published granule spacing.",
        "transfer_boundary: Chronospecies wavelengths are reconstructions, not measurements from True 1997 or Richards 2005.",
        "transfer_boundary: Richards 2005 is the pseudoobscura genome, used only as obscura-clade context for miranda." ;
    pk:anatomicalStructure "Turing pigment stripe / ocellus wavelength in Drosophila melanogaster" ;
    pk:aristotelianEfficientCause "1. Chemical Turing / RD" ;
    pk:aristotelianMegistonGenos "II. Anaima (Invertebrata)" ;
    pk:aristotelianPoionForm "Stripes, Spots & Ocelli" ;
    pk:aristotelianPosonLaw "Turing Wavenumber k_c" ;
    pk:aristotelianSubalternClass "Entoma (Arthropoda)" ;
    pk:biologicalGenus "Drosophila" ;
    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-melanogaster-turing-wavelength-s0.py; output: docs/media/drosophila_melanogaster_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png; organism: Drosophila melanogaster; environment: n/a; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Turing (1952) selects a finite wavelength by diffusion-driven instability. | Schnakenberg (1979) kinetics are f = a - u + u^2 v and g = b - u^2 v. | Wittkopp, True and Carroll (2002) place Drosophila melanin via Yellow and Ebony. | True et al. (1997) quantify morphological divergence of D. mauritiana from the simulans complex. | Richards et al. (2005) compare the D. pseudoobscura genome with D. melanogaster. | The Karwath photograph is an adult male D. melanogaster under CC BY-SA 2.5.; reconstructed_in_script: Gamma = 1.032078 is solved so argmax sigma(k) = 2 pi / 2.736 per micrometre. | Mauritiana and miranda wavelengths at that shared gamma, linear and mode-seeded. | Mask quantile sweep and the noise-seeded negative control. | Registration amplitude 0.16 on the Karwath photograph.; transfer_boundary: 2.736 µm is the assigned detail scale, not a published granule spacing. | Chronospecies wavelengths are reconstructions, not measurements from True 1997 or Richards 2005. | Richards 2005 is the pseudoobscura genome, used only as obscura-clade context for miranda.; does_not_claim: That adult abdominal stripes or ommatidia have wavelength 2.736 µm. | That broadband noise selects the linear critical wavelength. It does not, in the 1D control. | That the spot lattice is a photograph of an ocellus. | A second independent assessor, or a signed nanopub (no ~/.nanopub/profile.yml).]; phenomenon_size: 1.9 µm (1.919e-06 m, log10=-5.717 m, tier=3_subcellular_um); species_scale_ladder (10 runs from 1.9 µm to 4.3 mm): 1.9 µm:drosophila-affinis-bioelectric-polarity, 6.0 µm:drosophila-affinis-vertex-packing, 96 µm:drosophila-affinis-turing-wavelength, 192 µm:drosophila-affinis-clock-wavefront, 432 µm:drosophila-affinis-morphogen-condensation, 528 µm:drosophila-affinis-elastic-buckling, 600 µm:drosophila-affinis-flux-canalization, 840 µm:drosophila-affinis-branching-tree" ;
